// blackvault, full-content peer. The hub and black-pc.
//
// Install as ".stignore" in the vault root on any device that takes its vault
// content over Syncthing. Syncthing reloads it live, so a wrong copy here takes
// effect within a scan and is silent: the folder simply stops carrying content
// and still reports itself in sync.
//
// Everything ignored below is per-machine or regenerable. Everything else,
// including "99 - Meta/Agent State/.leases/", syncs.

// Machine-local git clone. Each device keeps its own.
/.git
// Agent tooling links and caches. Regenerable, and .codex/cache alone is 310M.
// Anchored at the root only: nested dirs like "99 - Meta/Skills/.opencode/"
// are real vault content and must sync.
/.codex
/.claude
/.opencode
/.agents
/.codegraph
// Per-machine Obsidian state. A pane layout and a LiveSync connection each
// belong to one device, so replicating them makes two machines fight over one
// file. These lines only ignore: stale copies already on disk are left alone.
/.obsidian/workspace.json
/.obsidian/workspace-mobile.json
/.obsidian/plugins/obsidian-livesync
// Obsidian and plugin caches. Regenerable.
/.smart-env
/.trash
// OS clutter. (?d) lets Syncthing delete these locally when they vanish remotely.
(?d).DS_Store
(?d)Thumbs.db
